course: dictionary
lesson: 14661
title: Preferential
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Preferential comes from prefer, which means to like one thing more than another. When you see preferential, look at the words around it for clues about who gets something better.
explain: «The teacher gave the older children preferential seats near the front.» The clues are older children and near the front. Everyone else sat further back, so preferential must mean better for some people than for others.
explain: Preferential treatment can feel unfair if you are not the one getting it. «Mia was annoyed that her brother got preferential treatment at dinner.» Test it: swap in better than others, and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Preferential means giving one person or group better treatment than others.
fact: Preferential is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as treatment, rates or seats.
fact: The phrase preferential treatment means special, better treatment for some people.
fact: In shops and money matters, preferential rates are lower or better prices for some customers.
fact: Prefer means to like one thing more than another, and preferential comes from it.
exercise: «The club gave its members preferential prices on tickets.» What does preferential mean here? | Tickets that cost nothing at all | Prices that are the same for everyone | Tickets sold only on a Monday | *Lower, better prices for members than for others
exercise: Ella says preferential means pretty. What does it mean? | Lost and alone | *Better treatment for one group than for others | Very pretty and soft | Quick and fast
exercise: Which phrase means special, better treatment for some people? | equal turns | equal shares | *preferential treatment | ordinary queue
test: «Some people thought the preferential seating was unfair to the others.» Why might the others think it was unfair? | Because the seats were broken | Because everyone got the same seats | Because nobody wanted to sit down | *Because some people got better seats than they did
test: Which word is the root of preferential? | refer | *prefer | prepare | pretend
exam: «The lifeguard gave the swimming club preferential use of the pool on Tuesdays.» What does preferential mean here? | *Better use of the pool for the club than for other people | The pool has no water in it | Equal use of the pool by everyone | The pool is closed all day
